                <pb facs="0479" n="389" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg389"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00 R 29/216: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wallace</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-05-18T17:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 18, 1920—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 18—1:24 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1169. B–91. For Davis. Supplementing my B–82.</p>
                <p>Commission decided yesterday ask all government[s] signing treaty, whether
                    ratified or not, to report to Commission what progress made in making up claims,
                    what doubtful questions upon which they desired rulings, nature of proof they
                    proposed to such [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>]; also to submit complete
                    files of evidence in specific cases of various kinds for consideration as test
                    cases, all for the purpose of enabling Commission to formulate regulations for
                    presentation of claims; also [to] request suggestion as to fixing definite time
                    limit for filing claims with Commission. Foregoing request not formal, but
                    merely practical useful preliminary for assistance work of Commission. Foregoing
                    for your information. Commission request when drafted will probably be sent to
                    Embassy. Boyden.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallace</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
